The output is basically the same as the comment that is about to be made. Here, the program checks the status of `New_Ret` and that whether or not the last index of `x` in the new list is not equal to the size of the old list. If the assertion doesn't hold true, an exception will be thrown.--------------------
Debug.Assert(New_Ret ? New_arrListLastIndexOfX != Old_arrListCount : true);
</code>

